  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let us assume that vectors are collinear so,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#8741;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Now, for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;to be non-collinear smallest positive integer will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So, mid-point of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>82</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
